; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Compliment Machine
; CATEGORY: Stories, Chatbots & Language
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     random, sentences, kindness, hearts
; SUMMARY:  Builds kind, silly compliments from three lists of word pieces and frames each one with hearts.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A compliment here has three parts: a start ("You are"), a
;   describing phrase ("as clever as") and a comparison ("a dolphin
;   doing math"). Picking one piece from each list gives hundreds of
;   different compliments, all of them nice. Type a name and the
;   compliment is addressed to that person, framed with hearts.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Run it and type the name of someone you want to cheer up (or your
;   own). You get three compliments. Type another name for more, or
;   QUIT to stop.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * multiplying choices: 5 starts x 6 middles x 7 endings
;   * drawing a heart from two arcs and two lines
;   * SENTENCE joining lists into one line
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Work out how many different compliments there are
;   * Add a list of things the person might be good at
; ============================================================

make "starts [[you are] [honestly, you are] [everyone agrees you are] [I think you are] [you are clearly]]
make "middles [[as clever as] [as kind as] [as bright as] [as brave as] [as cheerful as] [as wonderful as]]
make "endings [[a dolphin doing math] [a lighthouse on a stormy night] [a puppy with a new ball] [a rainbow after lunch] [the sun on a Saturday] [a dragon who bakes cookies] [a library full of comics]]

; WORD can only join words, so to put ! after a phrase we add it to
; the last word of the phrase.
to exclaim :phrase
  output lput word last :phrase "! butlast :phrase
end

to compliment :name
  output (sentence word :name ", pick :starts pick :middles exclaim pick :endings)
end

to heart :x :y :size :color
  ; Start at the bottom point and walk round the outline: a straight
  ; side, a half circle, a quarter turn at the dip, a half circle, and
  ; the other straight side back to the point.
  penup setxy :x :y setheading 45 setpencolor :color pendown
  filled :color [
    fd :size
    repeat 18 [fd :size * pi / 36 lt 10]
    rt 90
    repeat 18 [fd :size * pi / 36 lt 10]
    fd :size
  ]
  penup
end

to frame :lines
  clearscreen hideturtle
  repeat 14 [heart -380 + 55 * repcount 230 14 pick [4 5 12 13]]
  repeat 14 [heart -380 + 55 * repcount -280 14 pick [4 5 12 13]]
  setpencolor 13 setlabelheight 16
  localmake "y 100
  foreach :lines [penup setxy -360 :y label ? make "y :y - 70]
end

to cheer
  print []
  print [Who deserves a compliment? Type a name, or quit.]
  localmake "who readword
  if or emptyp :who memberp :who [quit stop q bye] [print [Have a lovely day.] stop]
  localmake "lines (list compliment :who compliment :who compliment :who)
  foreach :lines [print ?]
  frame :lines
  cheer
end

cheer
